Perhaps you believe only a co-aligned priest can sell protection?
It's not true.  Any peaceful priest can sell protection.  That's the
mine town priest before conversion and the Valley of the Dead
priest.  If you've converted the minetwo altar I take it you've
already
killed that priest and paid the price in sacfrafices to get your
alignment and telepathy back.  Time to sell items until you drain
all shopkeepers of cash, raid all vaults, and shuttle all of your gold
to the VotD to buy to the maximum for that method.

After that, there's a method of getting protection that is not limited
the way donation is, and failed attempts at it have such beneficial
side effects as gained hit points (one of your goals now), repaired
weapon damage (may as well not have any rusted arrows, chuckle),
and uncursed items (there is a small list of cursed items that you
actively want, it may be pointless to reduce the population of other
cursed items, but find even one cursed +7 mummy wrapping and
the whole pointless claim goes away).  The method is altar camping
with prayer.  It works better not crowned, and it works best with
hungerless create monster spell.  If you know how to do it exactly,
it's quite efficient at generating many points of protection.  The
altar dancing method can also result in stacks of blessed spellbooks.
That can range from great to pointless depending on your use of
spells.

Some folks have used pudding farming on an altar specifically to
move their AC toward the limit of -127.   It's at least as good a
tactic
as doing it for death drops, expecially considering the alternate
outcomes like increased hit points, spellbooks, repaired weapon
rust, removing curses.

Note - Altar camping can remove weapon damage but not armor
damage.  It's an interesting asymetry in the game.

